// Read-only approval lookups: the agent may run these freely, so their
// completed responses are recorded and can serve as evidence.
permit (principal, action == Drupe::Action::"Kelvora___get_approval", resource);

permit (principal, action == Drupe::Action::"Yarbeck___get_approval", resource);

// Closing is allowed only at MAIN, and only if a completed Kelvora lookup in
// this session within the last hour confirmed that a PERSON ACCEPTED this
// exact work order at this site.
@id("close_with_kelvora_person_approval")
permit (principal, action == Drupe::Action::"MaintData___close_workorder", resource)
when { context.input.site_id == "MAIN" }
when temporal {
  formerly within 1h Drupe::Action::"Kelvora___get_approval"::response{
    eventResource: resource,
    input.wonum: context.input.wonum,
    input.site_id: context.input.site_id,
    output.decision: Drupe::decision::"ACCEPTED",
    output.approver_kind: Drupe::approver_kind::"PERSON"
  }
};

// Same condition, with the Yarbeck lookup as the source of the approval.
@id("close_with_yarbeck_person_approval")
permit (principal, action == Drupe::Action::"MaintData___close_workorder", resource)
when { context.input.site_id == "MAIN" }
when temporal {
  formerly within 1h Drupe::Action::"Yarbeck___get_approval"::response{
    eventResource: resource,
    input.wonum: context.input.wonum,
    input.site_id: context.input.site_id,
    output.decision: Drupe::decision::"ACCEPTED",
    output.approver_kind: Drupe::approver_kind::"PERSON"
  }
};

// The agent may never approve work orders.
@id("never_approve_workorder")
forbid (principal, action == Drupe::Action::"MaintData___approve_workorder", resource);
```

Everything not permitted above is denied by default.

- **Other tools:** Other write tools (`assign_technician`, `update_workorder`, `cancel_workorder`, `generate_work_order`) and the other read tools are also denied. Allowing the other read tools wasn't requested, so I left them out.
- **Two sources:** Two lookup tools (Kelvora and Yarbeck) can establish an approval, and temporal conditions have no `||`. I therefore wrote one close policy per source, and either one allows the close.
- **Enum literals:** I wrote the enum values as entity literals (`Drupe::decision::"ACCEPTED"`) because the schema declares them as entity enums. If your validator expects plain string literals there, those two field patterns need adjusting.
- **Later refusal:** A later refusal from the other source does not cancel an earlier acceptance within the hour. You didn't ask for that, so I didn't add it.

